{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789326758,"nonce":"KA4XLHtKk5xaLZ7mQ6JRNU50CWU=","title":"Method call kernel: a boxed field round-trips GPR and FP registers every iteration","message":"caribou's interop benchmark (fixtures/src/bench/tally.wren, wrenMethod)\nloops `t.bump(1)` where bump does `_t = _t + x`. With the range loop\ncounted and bump inlined, the LLVM tier's loop is a load of the boxed\nfield, a Num check, fmov to FP, fadd, fmov back, store, plus the class\nguard and the field-kind note. Measured 5.5 ns per iteration on the Mac\n(load ~30) against Ash's 3.5 for the same loop; static call, getter,\nsetter and closure call sit at 1.0-1.2 and construct at 4.1.\n\nThe chain is store -\u003e next iteration's load (store forwarding) -\u003e fmov -\u003e\nfadd -\u003e fmov -\u003e store, about 15 cycles. The kind note was a read-modify-\nwrite on the class's byte every store; it is now a load and a compare\nwith the store only when the byte changes, and a receiver a dominating\nClassIs guard (or the backend's own splice check) proved gets the\nstatic note, which the compile elides once the byte records the kind\nbeing stored. That removed the RMW chain but only moved the loop from\n5.8 to 5.5: the field round trip is the cost.\n\nOptions, in order of payoff:\n1. Scalar replacement of a mutated non-escaping instance: `t` is fresh\n   (constructor inlined), its only uses are guarded get/set_field and a\n   trivial getter after the loop; keep `_t` in an f64 loop param and\n   materialise the object only on the slow paths (class-miss call,\n   generic construct when the module variable is not the class). The\n   sroa_loop pass covers immutable objects read through trivial getters;\n   this needs stores and materialisation. Expected ~1 ns like the static\n   and getter loops.\n2. Keep the field in the FP domain: load the slot once as i64 for the\n   check and once as double for the arithmetic, store the double. GVN\n   coerces the second load into a bitcast of the first, so this needs\n   the check moved off the value (per-field class invariant: the class\n   byte says the field only ever held Nums, so the load needs no check\n   and can be typed double). The invariant path exists for guarded\n   getter results (note_field_invariant + GuardNumAt) but not for\n   get_field inside a MIR-inlined body, which has no deopt point.","files":null}]}